{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is executing a stitch task (Task ID: 5514) for the go-unix-utils project. The task requires implementing srd079-base32 requirements R2.1, R2.2, R2.3, and R2.4 in `cmd/base32/main.go`. These requirements cover Base32 decoding functionality:\n   - R2.1: `-d` or `--decode` flag to decode Base32 input from FILE or stdin\n   - R2.2: Ignore whitespace during decoding\n   - R2.3: `-i` or `--ignore-garbage` flag to ignore non-alphabet characters during decoding\n   - R2.4: Exit 1 with stderr error when invalid Base32 characters encountered (without --ignore-garbage)\n   \n   Design decisions specify using `pkg/encutil.Decode` with `DecoderConfig` and extending existing flag parsing.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Base32 encoding/decoding per RFC 4648\n   - Differential testing against GNU reference binary (`gbase32`)\n   - `pkg/encutil` shared encoding/decoding library with `EncoderConfig`, `DecoderConfig`, `Encode()`, `Decode()`, `OpenInput()`\n   - SIGPIPE handler via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Manual CLI argument parsing (no cobra for this utility)\n   - Go's `encoding/base32.StdEncoding` for Base32 operations\n   - Execution constitution mandates: no git commands, 40-line function limit, SPDX header, write-all-then-build strategy\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd079-base32.yaml**\n     - Contains the full SRD for base32 with requirements R1 (Encoding), R2 (Decoding), R3 (Exit codes/SIGPIPE)\n     - R2.1-R2.4 are the specific requirements for this task\n     - Non-goals: no Base32hex, no Base64\n   \n   - **cmd/base32/main.go** (173 lines, existing implementation)\n     - This is the file to modify, but it ALREADY contains full R2.1-R2.4 implementation\n     - Full existing code:\n     ```go\n     // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     \n     package main\n     \n     import (\n         \"encoding/base32\"\n         \"errors\"\n         \"fmt\"\n         \"os\"\n         \"strconv\"\n         \"strings\"\n         \"syscall\"\n     \n         \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/encutil\"\n         \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n     )\n     \n     func main() {\n         sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n         opts, file := parseArgs(os.Args[1:])\n         rc, err := encutil.OpenInput(file)\n         if err != nil {\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"base32: %s: %s\\n\", file, err.Error())\n             os.Exit(1)\n         }\n         defer rc.Close()\n         if opts.decode {\n             err = encutil.Decode(rc, os.Stdout, encutil.DecoderConfig{\n                 Decode:        decodeBase32,\n                 IgnoreGarbage: opts.ignoreGarbage,\n             })\n         } else {\n             err = encutil.Encode(rc, os.Stdout, encutil.EncoderConfig{\n                 Encode:  encodeBase32,\n                 WrapCol: opts.wrap,\n             })\n         }\n         if err != nil {\n             if errors.Is(err, syscall.EPIPE) {\n                 os.Exit(0)\n             }\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"base32: %s\\n\", err.Error())\n             os.Exit(1)\n         }\n     }\n     \n     func encodeBase32(data []byte) string {\n         return base32.StdEncoding.EncodeToString(data)\n     }\n     \n     func decodeBase32(s string) ([]byte, error) {\n         return base32.StdEncoding.DecodeString(s)\n     }\n     \n     type options struct {\n         decode        bool\n         ignoreGarbage bool\n         wrap          int\n     }\n     \n     func parseArgs(args []string) (options, string) {\n         opts := options{wrap: 76}\n         var file string\n         i := 0\n         for i < len(args) {\n             arg := args[i]\n             if arg == \"--\" {\n                 if i+1 < len(args) {\n                     file = args[i+1]\n                 }\n                 break\n             }\n             if handled, advance := parseLongFlag(args[i:], &opts); handled {\n                 i += advance\n                 continue\n             }\n             if arg == \"-\" || !strings.HasPrefix(arg, \"-\") {\n                 file = arg\n                 i++\n                 continue\n             }\n             i += parseShortFlags(args[i:], &opts)\n         }\n         return opts, file\n     }\n     \n     func parseLongFlag(remaining []string, opts *options) (bool, int) {\n         arg := remaining[0]\n         if !strings.HasPrefix(arg, \"--\") {\n             return false, 0\n         }\n         if arg == \"--wrap\" || strings.HasPrefix(arg, \"--wrap=\") {\n             return parseWrapFlag(remaining, opts)\n         }\n         switch arg {\n         case \"--decode\":\n             opts.decode = true\n         case \"--ignore-garbage\":\n             opts.ignoreGarbage = true\n         default:\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"base32: unrecognized option '%s'\\n\", arg)\n             os.Exit(1)\n         }\n         return true, 1\n     }\n     \n     func parseWrapFlag(remaining []string, opts *options) (bool, int) {\n         arg := remaining[0]\n         if strings.HasPrefix(arg, \"--wrap=\") {\n             val := arg[len(\"--wrap=\"):]\n             n, err := strconv.Atoi(val)\n             if err != nil {\n                 fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"base32: invalid wrap size: '%s'\\n\", val)\n                 os.Exit(1)\n             }\n             opts.wrap = n\n             return true, 1\n         }\n         if len(remaining) < 2 {\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"base32: option '--wrap' requires an argument\\n\")\n             os.Exit(1)\n         }\n         n, err := strconv.Atoi(remaining[1])\n         if err != nil {\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"base32: invalid wrap size: '%s'\\n\", remaining[1])\n             os.Exit(1)\n         }\n         opts.wrap = n\n         return true, 2\n     }\n     \n     func parseShortFlags(remaining []string, opts *options) int {\n         arg := remaining[0]\n         flags := arg[1:]\n         for j := 0; j < len(flags); j++ {\n             switch flags[j] {\n             case 'd':\n                 opts.decode = true\n             case 'i':\n                 opts.ignoreGarbage = true\n             case 'w':\n                 val := flags[j+1:]\n                 if val != \"\" {\n                     n, err := strconv.Atoi(val)\n                     if err != nil {\n                         fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"base32: invalid wrap size: '%s'\\n\", val)\n                         os.Exit(1)\n                     }\n                     opts.wrap = n\n                     return 1\n                 }\n                 if len(remaining) < 2 {\n                     fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"base32: option requires an argument -- 'w'\\n\")\n                     os.Exit(1)\n                 }\n                 n, err := strconv.Atoi(remaining[1])\n                 if err != nil {\n                     fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"base32: invalid wrap size: '%s'\\n\", remaining[1])\n                     os.Exit(1)\n                 }\n                 opts.wrap = n\n                 return 2\n             default:\n                 fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"base32: invalid option -- '%c'\\n\", flags[j])\n                 os.Exit(1)\n             }\n         }\n         return 1\n     }\n     ```\n   \n   - **pkg/encutil/decode.go** (85 lines)\n     - Contains `DecoderConfig` struct, `Decode()` function, `stripWhitespace()`, `stripGarbage()`, `isEncodingAlphabet()`, `OpenInput()`\n     - Already handles R2.2 (whitespace stripping) and R2.3 (garbage ignoring) at the library level\n   \n   - **pkg/encutil/encode.go** (49 lines)\n     - C